    "created_at": "2016-04-21T18:43:13Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-04-21T18:43:13Z",
    "body": "Very interesting. I think we should make it explicit by inserting into https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/semantics.html#hyperlink-auditing between steps 2 and 3 a step that says\n\n> Optionally, abort these steps. (For example, a user agent might wish to disregard all URLs whose schemes are not http or https, since this feature makes little sense in that case; or, a user agent may wish to ignore URLs in accordance with the user's expressed preferences.)\n\nI'd also be happy to make that a normative requirement, but we should get the thoughts of other ping implementers. I'm going to tag in @mikewest since he recently worked on \"noopener\" in Blink which is kinda-sorta-vaguely related. Gecko has this but disabled by default...\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
