    "created_at": "2016-04-22T06:00:25Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-04-22T06:00:25Z",
    "body": "So the URL Standard defines \"network scheme\" which is ftp/http/https at the moment. ftp might die, but in case it doesn't, should we have a different term for just http/https? I was thinking \"HTTP scheme\" might be good enough, or would that be confusing?\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
