    "created_at": "2016-04-22T09:41:05Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-04-22T09:41:05Z",
    "body": "Should we ignore the value when sending the ping, or when setting the value of the attribute? I don't think there's significant impact either way, but the latter would ensure that only valid URLs were reflected if folks wanted to inspect the attribute at some point. Not sure that's worth the complexity...\n\nIn any event, locking things down to HTTP/HTTPS sounds fine to me. \n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
