    "created_at": "2016-04-25T10:35:07Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-04-25T10:35:07Z",
    "body": "I don't think it's useful for `ping` to have supported tokens. `supports()` was added to solve the problem of how to feature-check support for stuff. There's no use case for checking if pinging `blob:` works. If we ever add a new scheme that will be supported by `ping`, I suppose that could be feature-checked using the `URL` constructor?\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
